  "content" : "<p>A widget can read the whole site it lives in. This one draws every post on this site as a timeline, straight from <code>planet.json</code>, and updates itself every time the site is published.</p>\n<div id=\"timeline\" style=\"border:1px solid var(--foreground-secondary-color);padding:16px\">loading…</div>\n<p style=\"font-size:13px;opacity:.6\">How: twenty lines inline in the post, using <code>croptop.site()</code>. The same call can build an archive page, a tag cloud, or \"you might also like\".</p>\n<script type=\"module\">\ncroptop.ready(({ site }) => {\n  const el = document.getElementById(\"timeline\");\n  const posts = [...site.articles].sort((a, b) => a.created - b.created);\n  const toDate = (t) => new Date((t + 978307200) * 1000);\n  const first = toDate(posts[0].created), last = toDate(posts[posts.length - 1].created);\n  const span = Math.max(1, last - first);\n  el.innerHTML = `<div style=\"font-size:13px;opacity:.7\">${posts.length} posts between ${first.toLocaleDateString()} and ${last.toLocaleDateString()}</div>\n    <div style=\"position:relative;height:56px;margin:14px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--foreground-secondary-color)\"></div><ol style=\"margin:0;padding-left:18px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7\"></ol>`;\n  const track = el.children[1], list = el.children[2];\n  posts.forEach((p) => {\n    const x = (toDate(p.created) - first) / span * 100;\n    const dot = document.createElement(\"a\"); dot.href = croptop.prefix + p.id + \"/\"; dot.title = p.title || \"untitled\";\n    dot.style.cssText = `position:absolute;left:calc(${x}% - 6px);bottom:-6px;width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;background:${p.id === croptop.postId ? \"#3bb273\" : \"var(--link-color)\"}`;\n    track.appendChild(dot);\n    const li = document.createElement(\"li\"); li.innerHTML = `<a href=\"${croptop.prefix}${p.id}/\">${p.title || \"untitled\"}</a> <span style=\"opacity:.5\">${toDate(p.created).toLocaleDateString()}</span>`;\n    list.appendChild(li);\n  });\n});\n</script>\n",
